WEBVTT

00:00:02.860 --> 00:00:07.290
As expected, the first battle was a series of close calls. However,

00:00:08.780 --> 00:00:12.820
the children who have started
to walk are now running on their own.

00:00:15.070 --> 00:00:18.440
For now, they lock their hesitations within their hearts.

00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:23.040
From now on, they will continue fighting together as a team.

00:00:23.640 --> 00:00:28.780
Together with their partners and their comrades, they’ll face the upcoming battles head-on.

00:00:30.100 --> 00:00:34.510
At many different places, they’ll fight many different battles.

00:00:34.510 --> 00:00:39.420
Magical Girl Lyrical Nanoha StrikerS<i>
will now begin.</i>

00:02:35.900 --> 00:02:41.970
Our debut was May 13, the unit’s first emergency deployment.

00:02:43.930 --> 00:02:47.300
A Lost Logia was being transported along a smuggling route.

00:02:47.300 --> 00:02:52.320
A Relic was discovered by Gadgets that had attacked the Linear Rail carrying it.

00:02:52.320 --> 00:02:56.680
The mission was to obstruct them and recover the Relic.

00:02:56.680 --> 00:03:01.270
Due to the actions of each of Riot Force 6’s members at the time, the problem was safely resolved.

00:03:02.740 --> 00:03:10.920
The recovered Serial No. IX Relic is now protected and being investigated in the Central Laboratory.

00:03:10.920 --> 00:03:14.960
Our first mission was more or less problem-free and a good start,

00:03:14.960 --> 00:03:18.300
according to Commander Hayate and Riot Force 6’s superiors,

00:03:18.300 --> 00:03:23.500
Knight Carim and Admiral Chrono, who seemed to be satisfied...

00:03:23.500 --> 00:03:24.790
Command Sergeant Major Rein.

00:03:26.730 --> 00:03:27.550
Shari!

00:03:27.550 --> 00:03:29.640
Are you on your break?

00:03:29.640 --> 00:03:33.160
Half on break, half working.

00:03:34.070 --> 00:03:36.780
I was writing my personal service log.

00:03:37.490 --> 00:03:38.440
I see.

00:03:39.480 --> 00:03:40.810
What about you, Shari?

00:03:40.810 --> 00:03:45.410
I just got back from checking the condition of the new Devices at the training grounds.

00:03:45.410 --> 00:03:49.300
Is that so? Is everyone doing well?

00:03:49.300 --> 00:03:53.580
Yes. The forwards and the Devices couldn’t be any better!

00:03:56.500 --> 00:03:58.420
All right, here I come!

00:04:00.800 --> 00:04:02.510
Mach Caliber!

00:04:02.510 --> 00:04:03.950
Protection

00:04:22.870 --> 00:04:24.910
That hurts.

00:04:24.910 --> 00:04:29.920
I see. Your barrier strength doesn’t seem to be that bad after all.

00:04:30.860 --> 00:04:32.740
Thank you, ma’am.

00:04:34.450 --> 00:04:38.700
My position, like yours, is the front attacker.

00:04:38.700 --> 00:04:45.050
Cutting through enemy lines unaided
and leading the defensive line is our duty.

00:04:45.050 --> 00:04:48.000
With greater defensive and survival capabilities,

00:04:48.000 --> 00:04:53.730
you can attack longer and won’t require help from support units.

00:04:53.730 --> 00:04:56.050
Nanoha has taught you this, correct?

00:04:56.050 --> 00:04:57.900
Yes, Lt. Vita.

00:04:57.900 --> 00:04:59.970
Barrier magic to nullify hits,

00:04:59.970 --> 00:05:02.310
shield magic to repel them,

00:05:02.310 --> 00:05:05.820
and field magic to surround yourself for protection.

00:05:05.820 --> 00:05:08.610
Learn to master these three types.

00:05:08.610 --> 00:05:10.220
And to avoid being pushed back,

00:05:10.220 --> 00:05:14.400
work on your lower body stance and learn to utilize Mach Caliber.

00:05:14.400 --> 00:05:15.760
I’ll do my best!

00:05:15.990 --> 00:05:17.360
I’ll learn.

00:05:17.710 --> 00:05:22.170
Attacks that crush defenses are my specialty.

00:05:23.840 --> 00:05:28.800
So unless you want to get smashed by Graf Eisen,
you’d better defend well.

00:05:28.800 --> 00:05:30.260
Yes, ma’am!

00:05:30.260 --> 00:05:34.680
Erio and Caro, you aren’t as sturdy as the likes of Subaru and Vita.

00:05:34.680 --> 00:05:37.600
Therefore, reaction and evasion are most important.

00:05:37.600 --> 00:05:38.900
For example...

00:05:40.860 --> 00:05:42.780
In this way, like this.

00:05:44.240 --> 00:05:46.570
Firstly, move around so they cannot aim.

00:05:48.980 --> 00:05:50.910
If you are somewhere exposed to attack,

00:05:52.240 --> 00:05:53.540
don’t stay there long.

00:05:55.120 --> 00:05:55.830
Got it?

00:05:55.830 --> 00:05:56.870
Yes, ma’am!

00:05:56.870 --> 00:05:59.700
If you can do this perfectly at a slow pace,

00:06:00.660 --> 00:06:02.170
we’ll increase the speed.

00:06:15.020 --> 00:06:16.040
Something like this, okay?

00:06:24.150 --> 00:06:26.620
A-Amazing.

00:06:27.570 --> 00:06:33.060
That was a basic move that anyone
can do with practice, just done very quickly.

00:06:33.060 --> 00:06:34.570
Y-Yes, ma’am!

00:06:34.570 --> 00:06:39.540
At faster speeds, relying solely on
your intuition while moving becomes dangerous.

00:06:39.990 --> 00:06:45.620
Erio, as a guard wing, you should be able to attack and support from any position.

00:06:45.620 --> 00:06:51.120
Caro, as a full back, you should be able to move swiftly and aid your comrades.

00:06:51.120 --> 00:06:56.180
Make sure you learn the basics of effective evasion.

00:06:56.180 --> 00:06:57.020
Yes, ma’am!

00:07:02.860 --> 00:07:05.180
Yes, that’s good, Teana.

00:07:05.180 --> 00:07:06.530
Just like that.

00:07:06.530 --> 00:07:07.480
Yes, ma’am!

00:07:08.310 --> 00:07:10.440
Shooter-types like you, Teana,

00:07:10.440 --> 00:07:13.270
who have to stand upright mustn’t dodge and defend against every attack,

00:07:13.270 --> 00:07:15.180
or they can’t do their jobs.

00:07:15.830 --> 00:07:16.570
Barret!

00:07:16.570 --> 00:07:18.750
Left: V. Right: R.F.

00:07:18.750 --> 00:07:19.320
Alert!

00:07:22.580 --> 00:07:26.090
Look, if you move like that,
you’ll never be able to stop guarding.

00:07:26.620 --> 00:07:28.040
Barret V. & R.F.

00:07:38.380 --> 00:07:39.560
Yes, that’s it!

00:07:39.560 --> 00:07:41.990
Stand firmly and widen your field of vision.

00:07:43.150 --> 00:07:45.070
What’s the essence of being a marksman?

00:07:45.070 --> 00:07:49.430
To select the correct bullet for
your opponent and strike them down.

00:07:50.530 --> 00:07:52.510
Quick judgment and accurate shooting!

00:07:52.510 --> 00:07:53.900
Reload

00:07:53.900 --> 00:07:58.700
To stand in the middle of the team and engage in mid-to-long-range battles faster than anyone.

00:07:58.700 --> 00:08:03.670
Teana, that’s the duty of our position, the center guard.

00:08:03.670 --> 00:08:04.550
Yes, ma’am!

00:08:08.150 --> 00:08:10.850
They’re really into it, aren’t they?

00:08:10.850 --> 00:08:13.880
Their first deployment seems to have been good motivation for them.

00:08:13.880 --> 00:08:17.200
Isn’t it nice for the young ones.

00:08:17.200 --> 00:08:20.110
They may be young, but they are developing quickly.

00:08:20.110 --> 00:08:23.220
It’ll still be a bit dangerous for a while.

00:08:23.220 --> 00:08:24.580
That’s for sure.

00:08:24.580 --> 00:08:27.890
Siggy, you aren’t going to participate?

00:08:27.890 --> 00:08:30.530
It’s because I’m an old-school knight.

00:08:31.250 --> 00:08:37.820
Unlike Subaru and Erio who use Mid-style or Modern Belkan, I work differently.

00:08:37.820 --> 00:08:43.960
And wielding but a sword, I have nothing to teach rear-line fighters like Teana and Caro.

00:08:43.960 --> 00:08:49.160
Not to mention, I’ve never been one to teach others.

00:08:49.160 --> 00:08:53.820
The only tactic I could teach them is how to get within range and slice the enemy. That’s about it.

00:08:54.720 --> 00:08:57.510
That’s an amazing argument you’ve prepared, you know.

00:08:57.510 --> 00:09:01.970
But you’re right, it’s probably a little too early for them.

00:09:03.370 --> 00:09:05.900
All right, that’s all for this morning’s training.

00:09:08.310 --> 00:09:10.260
Thanks for your hard work.

00:09:10.260 --> 00:09:13.500
Individual-skills training is a little bit tough, isn’t it?

00:09:13.500 --> 00:09:15.720
I don’t know about “a little.”

00:09:15.720 --> 00:09:17.240
More like “a lot.”

00:09:17.240 --> 00:09:21.820
Captain Fate is busy, so she will only be around once in a while.

00:09:21.820 --> 00:09:25.460
However, I’ll almost always be around.

00:09:25.460 --> 00:09:28.130
T-Thank you, ma’am.

00:09:28.130 --> 00:09:33.450
Also, this is mostly for the two Lightning members,
but it also applies to the two Stars:

00:09:33.450 --> 00:09:39.060
As your bodies are still in the midst of developing,
please be careful not to overdo it.

00:09:39.060 --> 00:09:39.800
Yes, ma’am!

00:09:39.800 --> 00:09:41.960
In that case, why don’t we have lunch?

00:09:41.960 --> 00:09:42.720
Yes, ma’am!

00:09:47.100 --> 00:09:49.020
Everyone’s been working hard!

00:09:49.020 --> 00:09:49.770
Yes, ma’am!

00:09:49.770 --> 00:09:52.470
Hayate, Rein, are you going out?

00:09:52.470 --> 00:09:54.600
Yes indeedy, Vita!

00:09:54.600 --> 00:09:58.450
Yeah, we’re going to the central region to talk with Major Nakajima.

00:09:59.300 --> 00:10:03.330
Subaru, do you have anything you want me to tell your father or sister?

00:10:04.200 --> 00:10:06.000
No, that’s all right.

00:10:07.920 --> 00:10:10.990
Well then, Hayate, Rein, have a safe trip.

00:10:10.990 --> 00:10:14.060
Give Major Nakajima and Ginga my regards.

00:10:14.060 --> 00:10:14.840
I will!

00:10:14.840 --> 00:10:17.300
Off we go!

00:10:17.300 --> 00:10:23.510
I understand, Subaru, that your father and sister are with the Ground Armed Service.

00:10:23.510 --> 00:10:30.200
Yeah, apparently Commander Yagami trained with Dad’s battalion for a while.

00:10:31.390 --> 00:10:35.650
But still, our unit has a lot of connections.

00:10:35.650 --> 00:10:39.070
The captains were childhood friends, right?

00:10:39.070 --> 00:10:44.290
That’s right. Nanoha and Commander Yagami
are from the same world.

00:10:45.530 --> 00:10:49.500
Fate lived there when she was younger, too.

00:10:51.190 --> 00:10:54.200
If I remember correctly, it’s Non-Administrated World #97.

00:10:54.200 --> 00:10:54.710
That’s right.

00:10:54.710 --> 00:11:00.260
This #97 is apparently where my dad’s ancestors come from.

00:11:00.260 --> 00:11:01.970
Is that right?

00:11:04.680 --> 00:11:10.100
That’s right! Your name sounds somewhat similar to Nanoha’s and the rest.

00:11:10.100 --> 00:11:15.990
Dad and I have never been to that world. I don’t really know anything about it.

00:11:17.360 --> 00:11:20.530
Now that you mention it, Erio, where were you from again?

00:11:21.530 --> 00:11:23.990
I was raised at the Main Office.

00:11:23.990 --> 00:11:27.790
The Bureau’s Main Office? Like the housing area?

00:11:27.790 --> 00:11:33.690
The Main Office’s protection facility for special kids.
I was there until I was eight years old.

00:11:33.690 --> 00:11:34.380
Jackass!

00:11:36.080 --> 00:11:39.040
Uh, hey, please don’t worry about it.

00:11:39.040 --> 00:11:41.160
They were nice there.

00:11:41.160 --> 00:11:44.040
And I led a normal, happy life.

00:11:44.040 --> 00:11:50.170
Oh yeah, that’s right! Ever since then, Fate has been your guardian, right, Erio?

00:11:50.170 --> 00:11:54.930
Yep! Even since before I can remember,
she’s done a lot for me.

00:11:54.930 --> 00:11:59.280
Ever since I started learning magic, she’d teach me once in a while.

00:11:59.280 --> 00:12:02.730
Honestly, she was always nice to me.

00:12:02.730 --> 00:12:07.740
Even now, I feel like Fate’s still raising me.

00:12:07.740 --> 00:12:13.690
When Fate was a child, something happened in her household that made her feel a bit lonely.

00:12:14.120 --> 00:12:19.650
Apparently that’s why she can’t leave lonely or sad children alone.

00:12:19.650 --> 00:12:25.610
Because she was saved by kind, warm hands as well.

00:12:42.360 --> 00:12:46.440
Your new unit seems to be doing rather well.

00:12:46.440 --> 00:12:49.280
Indeed, for now at least.

00:12:49.280 --> 00:12:51.400
So what’s the matter today?

00:12:51.400 --> 00:12:55.750
You wouldn’t have time to come all the way here
just to see your old acquaintances.

00:12:56.850 --> 00:12:59.990
Your favorite pupil has just a bit of a favor to ask of her teacher.

00:13:01.020 --> 00:13:01.600
Enter.

00:13:03.200 --> 00:13:04.740
Excuse me.

00:13:04.740 --> 00:13:05.910
Ginga!

00:13:05.910 --> 00:13:09.510
Lt. Colonel Yagami, long time no see!

00:13:11.180 --> 00:13:14.690
What I wanted to ask of you is about the investigation of smuggling routes.

00:13:14.690 --> 00:13:17.430
For the Lost Logia in your care?

00:13:17.430 --> 00:13:21.060
There are many different routes they could be using.

00:13:21.060 --> 00:13:26.070
For the specifics, Rein has brought the data and will give it to you later.

00:13:26.070 --> 00:13:29.520
Well, I don’t mind you using our investigation unit,

00:13:29.520 --> 00:13:33.030
since investigating smuggling is our main job anyway.

00:13:33.030 --> 00:13:35.380
You can ask for a favor, but...

00:13:35.380 --> 00:13:36.500
Please, if you would.

00:13:36.500 --> 00:13:38.000
You know, Yagami,

00:13:38.000 --> 00:13:40.750
instead of going to another Riot Force
or the Main Office’s investigations unit,

00:13:40.750 --> 00:13:42.520
you purposely came all the way here to see <i>me</i> about it.

00:13:42.520 --> 00:13:44.170
Is there any reason for that?

00:13:44.170 --> 00:13:48.250
I’ve also requested them to investigate the smuggling routes.

00:13:48.250 --> 00:13:52.330
But after all, the G.A.S. would know the area here the best.

00:13:53.770 --> 00:13:55.990
Well, I see your reasoning.

00:13:57.220 --> 00:13:59.090
Sure, we’ll take it.

00:13:59.090 --> 00:14:00.730
Thank you very much!

00:14:00.730 --> 00:14:04.810
The lead investigator is Cultus, and Ginga is his adjutant.

00:14:04.810 --> 00:14:08.980
Since you both know each other,
you should be able to work with Ginga easily.

00:14:08.980 --> 00:14:11.120
Okay, and on our side,

00:14:11.120 --> 00:14:14.230
Enforcer Testarossa-Harlaown will be in charge of the investigation,

00:14:14.230 --> 00:14:17.460
so Ginga would be able to work with her easily.

00:14:19.370 --> 00:14:21.980
I see, so Fate is...

00:14:21.980 --> 00:14:22.840
Righty-o!

00:14:22.840 --> 00:14:28.300
She’s Riot Force 6’s lead investigator,
so you might get to work together on the investigation.

00:14:28.300 --> 00:14:31.280
I’ll have to really try my best then!

00:14:31.280 --> 00:14:32.130
Yes!

00:14:32.130 --> 00:14:33.140
Oh, that’s right!

00:14:33.140 --> 00:14:33.810
Huh?

00:14:33.810 --> 00:14:39.510
Since you’re going to help with the investigation, Riot Force 6 will give you a Device as a gift.

00:14:39.510 --> 00:14:40.640
A Device?

00:14:40.640 --> 00:14:45.480
The same model as the one that was made for Subaru.
Of course, we’ll tune her for your use.

00:14:45.480 --> 00:14:49.950
For that... I’m really happy, but is that okay?

00:14:49.950 --> 00:14:56.250
No problem! To make sure you can accompany Fate,
we’ll make you an awesome Device!

00:14:56.250 --> 00:14:59.150
Thank you very much, Command Sergeant Major Rein!

00:15:01.000 --> 00:15:07.660
Having Subaru and now Ginga
come over makes me a feel a bit bad.

00:15:07.660 --> 00:15:14.720
Why? Subaru decided herself,
and Ginga would be happy to work with Miss Harlaown.

00:15:14.720 --> 00:15:15.430
Okay.

00:15:15.430 --> 00:15:19.760
But anyway, before I knew it, you became my superior.

00:15:19.760 --> 00:15:22.730
Provisional assistant mages sure rise up in rank quickly.

00:15:22.730 --> 00:15:26.130
A mage’s insignia is simply for decoration.

00:15:26.130 --> 00:15:30.550
At the Main Office and Central Command,
even junior officers treat me like a little girl.

00:15:30.550 --> 00:15:31.720
I can see that.

00:15:31.720 --> 00:15:35.120
Oh yeah, sorry about that!
I’m treating you like a little girl, too.

00:15:35.120 --> 00:15:40.040
Major Nakajima, you always were
and still are my superior who I respect.

00:15:40.860 --> 00:15:42.020
I see.

00:15:43.290 --> 00:15:46.300
Excuse me, this is First Lieutenant Lat Cultus.

00:15:46.300 --> 00:15:50.250
Hey, Lt. Colonel Yagami has a request for our assistance on a mission.

00:15:50.250 --> 00:15:53.860
Take Ginga to the conference room, and we’ll hold the meeting there.

00:15:53.860 --> 00:15:55.250
Understood, sir.

00:15:56.440 --> 00:15:57.500
And so you have it.

00:15:57.500 --> 00:16:00.230
All right. Thank you very much.

00:16:00.230 --> 00:16:03.190
After the meeting, want to go get something to eat?

00:16:03.190 --> 00:16:05.610
Sure, I’ll accompany you.

00:16:11.060 --> 00:16:13.240
That’s all the data we have on the Relic.

00:16:13.240 --> 00:16:15.670
They’ve properly sealed it, right?

00:16:15.670 --> 00:16:18.160
Yes, ma’am, and very securely at that.

00:16:18.160 --> 00:16:23.050
But still, I don’t really understand the reason Relics exist.

00:16:24.080 --> 00:16:28.920
There are too many traits that don’t make any sense for crystallized energy,

00:16:28.920 --> 00:16:31.510
and they’re too odd to be used as a power generator.

00:16:31.510 --> 00:16:36.670
Well, if their use was easily known, then they wouldn’t be Lost Logia.

00:16:39.850 --> 00:16:42.120
Is this the data from the Gadget’s remains?

00:16:42.120 --> 00:16:43.190
Yes, ma’am.

00:16:43.190 --> 00:16:48.090
These are the same as the ones captured by Signum and Vita.

00:16:49.110 --> 00:16:52.880
The new models aren’t very different internally.

00:16:53.770 --> 00:16:55.350
Hmm? Something wrong?

00:16:55.350 --> 00:16:58.230
Go back a bit! To that picture of the Type 3’s remains.

00:16:58.230 --> 00:16:59.230
O-Okay.

00:16:59.230 --> 00:17:01.830
Probably the internal processing unit.

00:17:01.830 --> 00:17:05.040
Which would be... around here?

00:17:05.040 --> 00:17:06.270
That’s it.

00:17:06.270 --> 00:17:10.000
Is this a jewel? An energy crystal of some sort?

00:17:10.000 --> 00:17:11.960
A Jewel Seed.

00:17:11.960 --> 00:17:15.920
Back in the day, Nanoha and I
were searching for and collecting them.

00:17:15.920 --> 00:17:19.790
Now, they should be under
the administration of the Bureau as Lost Logia.

00:17:19.790 --> 00:17:21.660
Now I get it.

00:17:21.660 --> 00:17:23.490
And why are those things <i>there?</i>

00:17:23.490 --> 00:17:27.680
Shari, magnify this area. Something’s written there.

00:17:27.680 --> 00:17:28.180
Okay.

00:17:29.380 --> 00:17:31.370
Is this a name?

00:17:31.370 --> 00:17:32.070
J...

00:17:32.070 --> 00:17:34.060
Jail Scaglietti.

00:17:37.160 --> 00:17:40.050
Dr. Jail Scaglietti.

00:17:40.050 --> 00:17:44.320
Starting with incidents relating to Lost Logia,
he’s committed an uncountable number of crimes,

00:17:44.320 --> 00:17:46.620
and a wide-area arrest warrant has been issued.

00:17:46.620 --> 00:17:49.410
He’s an interdimensional criminal on the most-wanted list.

00:17:49.410 --> 00:17:51.340
Interdimensional criminal?

00:17:51.340 --> 00:17:56.910
There was a bit of an incident,
and I’ve been chasing him for many years.

00:17:56.910 --> 00:18:01.680
Why would a criminal like him go through all the trouble to show that he’s responsible with such easy hints?

00:18:01.680 --> 00:18:06.660
If it’s really him, then he’s provoking us.
If it’s someone else, then they’re aiming to mislead us.

00:18:06.660 --> 00:18:11.270
Either way, they know that Nanoha and I are involved in this case.

00:18:11.270 --> 00:18:19.470
But if it <i>is</i> Scaglietti, I believe he would be capable of utilizing Lost Logia to manufacture Gadgets,

00:18:19.470 --> 00:18:22.570
and I can think of a couple of reasons he’d go after Relics.

00:18:22.570 --> 00:18:23.700
His reasons?

00:18:23.700 --> 00:18:27.530
Shari, get this data together,
and let’s get back to our base quickly.

00:18:27.530 --> 00:18:30.530
I want to gather the captains and hold an emergency meeting.

00:18:30.530 --> 00:18:32.360
Yes, ma’am, I’ll do it straightaway.

00:18:38.050 --> 00:18:42.000
Okay, roger that. I’ll return immediately,
and we’ll hold a countermeasures meeting.

00:18:42.000 --> 00:18:45.300
I’ve just requested some
extra help with the investigation, too.

00:18:46.930 --> 00:18:48.730
In that case, see you later.

00:18:50.020 --> 00:18:51.590
Was there a new development?

00:18:51.590 --> 00:18:55.360
We might have a clue as to who’s behind all of this.

00:18:56.440 --> 00:19:02.060
And so, I’m sorry, Major Nakajima. I’ll have to take my leave here.

00:19:04.230 --> 00:19:05.190
You can’t!

00:19:05.190 --> 00:19:07.070
Hurry up and get going.

00:19:07.070 --> 00:19:08.710
Your subordinates are waiting, right?

00:19:08.710 --> 00:19:13.470
Okay. Ginga, either Fate or I will contact you later, all right?

00:19:13.470 --> 00:19:15.170
Okay, I’ll be waiting.

00:19:17.400 --> 00:19:21.420
Dr. Scaglietti, was it? The criminal with a wide-area arrest warrant?

00:19:21.420 --> 00:19:22.010
Yes.

00:19:22.010 --> 00:19:25.250
You said you knew some reasons why he would be searching for the Relics.

00:19:25.250 --> 00:19:26.880
Would you name some?

00:19:26.880 --> 00:19:29.630
As the title <i>Doctor</i> suggests,

00:19:29.630 --> 00:19:34.980
he has abnormal passion and skill with biological research and manipulation.

00:19:34.980 --> 00:19:41.050
He even created a vast number of Gadgets to search for the Relics.

00:20:04.580 --> 00:20:08.420
Zest and Lutecia have resumed their activities.

00:20:09.660 --> 00:20:11.600
What about the client’s instructions?

00:20:11.600 --> 00:20:18.020
“Don’t send any help without their authorization if you can help it,” was his message.

00:20:18.020 --> 00:20:24.480
Once in their autonomous mode,
the Gadget Drones are not under my complete control.

00:20:24.480 --> 00:20:29.730
If they gather at a Relic, I wish he would let them pass.

00:20:29.730 --> 00:20:31.200
I’ll let him know.

00:20:31.200 --> 00:20:36.170
If they are going to act,
then I shall take my time observing them.

00:20:36.170 --> 00:20:43.000
They are important experimental Relic weapons, after all.

00:20:59.560 --> 00:21:03.280
Okay! That’s it for tonight’s training.

00:21:03.280 --> 00:21:06.200
Thank you, ma’am.

00:21:09.270 --> 00:21:11.120
Thanks for your hard work.

00:21:11.120 --> 00:21:12.340
Okay.

00:21:12.340 --> 00:21:14.010
Make sure to get a proper sleep.

00:21:14.010 --> 00:21:14.830
Yes, ma’am.

00:21:19.170 --> 00:21:25.290
But still, you really stay with them from morning to night, huh?

00:21:25.290 --> 00:21:26.670
Isn’t it tiring?

00:21:26.670 --> 00:21:30.890
I am Riot Force 6’s combat instructor after all. It’s a given.

00:21:30.890 --> 00:21:37.090
And about that, is it really okay to be so lenient with them?

00:21:37.090 --> 00:21:44.810
When we had our initial training, we were strictly trained in everything from walking to greetings.

00:21:44.810 --> 00:21:49.820
Anywhere you go, combat training is basically like this.

00:21:49.820 --> 00:21:54.490
If there’s time to scold and yell at them for little things,

00:21:54.490 --> 00:22:00.900
then that time should be spent in mock battle, teaching them precisely and thoroughly that way.

00:22:00.900 --> 00:22:04.360
I was told that a lot while at the instruction squad.

00:22:04.360 --> 00:22:06.380
Is that a lesson? Seriously?

00:22:07.590 --> 00:22:12.920
What we’re doing isn’t teaching and raising completely new recruits.

00:22:14.390 --> 00:22:18.760
We’re guiding mages who have the will and determination to become stronger

00:22:18.760 --> 00:22:23.140
and teaching them combat techniques that are higher than their current level,

00:22:23.140 --> 00:22:24.930
because we are combat instructors.

00:22:24.930 --> 00:22:30.620
Well, in any case, it’s pretty tough being an instructor.

00:22:30.620 --> 00:22:33.280
But you’re doing well too, Vita.

00:22:33.280 --> 00:22:35.250
Very well indeed.

00:22:35.250 --> 00:22:37.380
Don’t pet me!

00:22:38.570 --> 00:22:40.170
What’s wrong with you?

00:22:44.050 --> 00:22:49.480
Could you organize and store
today’s combat data in the data warehouse?

00:22:49.670 --> 00:22:50.820
All right.

00:22:52.390 --> 00:22:54.350
Thanks a lot, Raising Heart.

00:22:55.510 --> 00:22:58.730
It’ll probably be a while before these guys
realize how fortunate they are.

00:23:00.640 --> 00:23:01.780
Caro, they’re still on.

00:23:02.430 --> 00:23:03.730
Oops, that’s not good.

00:23:06.190 --> 00:23:08.950
It pisses me off hearing that from you.

00:23:08.950 --> 00:23:09.610
There, there.

00:23:09.610 --> 00:23:16.040
I’m Stars’s lieutenant, so I’ll protect you.

00:23:19.110 --> 00:23:19.830
What is it?

00:23:19.830 --> 00:23:23.530
It’s nothing! Let’s go, Nanoha.

00:23:23.530 --> 00:23:24.990
Okay, Vita.

00:25:18.530 --> 00:25:19.780
In the next mission,

00:25:19.780 --> 00:25:20.780
we will be acting
as hotel security,

00:25:20.780 --> 00:25:21.790
protecting the auction.

00:25:21.790 --> 00:25:26.330
Gadgets will be targeting the auction together with a mysterious summoning mage.

00:25:32.540 --> 00:25:34.420
Take off!
